OL,3,GNEWSAWhat is it like to be Jewish and
OL,4,Aliving in Ireland?
OL,5,
OL,6,FNaomi Handler has called Ireland home
OL,7,Ffor two decades.
OL,9,FShe's among the estimated 2,000 Jewish
OL,10,Fpeople living in the country - but has
OL,11,Fquestioned her place in it over the
OL,12,Fpast three years.
OL,14,FA mezuzah, a parchment scroll with a
OL,15,Fprayer from the Torah, common in Jewish
OL,16,Fhomes, hangs by her front door. "Should
OL,17,FI remove it?" she asks.
OL,19,FShe is one of a number of Jews who say
OL,20,Ftheir experiences of life in the
OL,21,FRepublic of Ireland have changed since
OL,22,Fthe war in Gaza began.
OL,23,APub: 20-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
